**Optimizing interpolation performance**

I’m considering using grid adaptive and high precision interpolation to achieve a residual of less than or equal to 1e-8 for final results. It’s really important to interpolate delta instead of ratios since normal differences can be small, and low n could lead to cancellation issues. There’s also a thought about compressing phonon convolutions into frequency-dependent P×P matrices to eliminate the FFT cost, transforming convolution into a spectral multiplication with a combined kernel spectrum.
